course: dictionary
lesson: 4988
title: Indicators: signs that show
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An indicator is something that shows or points to what is happening or what is true. Think of it as a sign. «An indicator is a substance whose colour shows whether something is acidic or alkaline.» The colour is the sign that tells you the answer.
explain: On a car or bike, an indicator is the flashing light that shows which way the vehicle will turn. «The indicator ticks before a turn» so other road users know what you plan to do. Cyclists use hand signals as indicators too.
explain: In science, an indicator is a substance that changes colour to show whether something is an acid or an alkali. Ask yourself: what is the colour telling me? If your idea of the word still makes sense when you put it into the sentence, you are on the right track.
fact: An indicator is a sign that shows or points to what is happening or what is true.
fact: «Litmus paper, made from lichens, turns red in acid and blue in alkali.»
fact: A car's indicator is a flashing light that shows which way the vehicle will turn.
fact: Phrases you may hear are universal indicator, litmus indicator, and «a good indicator of».
fact: Red cabbage juice can be used as an indicator to show whether something is an acid or an alkali.
exercise: «An indicator is a substance whose colour shows whether something is acidic or alkaline.» What does this indicator show? | How heavy something is | The weather for next week | *Whether something is an acid or an alkali | How loud something sounds
exercise: On a car, what does the indicator show? | *Which way the vehicle will turn | How fast the car is going | When the engine is hot | Who is driving the car
exercise: «Litmus paper turns red in acid and blue in alkali.» Find and copy the word that names the colour in acid. | paper | *red | alkali | litmus
test: In science, what does an indicator change to show the answer? | Sound | Size | *Colour | Weight
test: Temperature is an indicator of the season. What does this mean? | *It shows a trend that tells you about the season | It stops the season from changing | It is a type of season | It is a kind of thermometer that only measures rain
exam: A pool keeper checks the water with drops and a colour card. Why is this an indicator? | *It shows by its colour what the water is like | It changes the water into juice | It measures how many people swim | It cools the water down
